From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:15:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #4156] Keep reads through a pointer to volatile after a
 store

'*p = v; return *p;' with p pointing to a volatile object returned v without
reading the object again. Common subexpression elimination forwards the
stored value to a later read through the same pointer, and its volatility
check looked at the pointer operand, which is not volatile; what it points
to is.

No regression test: a read that returns what was just written cannot be
told from no read at run time in the simulator setup of the test suite.
Checked in the generated code for xdata and generic pointers: the read is
back, two reads stay two reads, and a pointer to a non-volatile object still
gets the store forwarded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/SDCCcse.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/SDCCcse.c b/src/SDCCcse.c
index 9c7395167..9dde24178 100644
--- a/src/SDCCcse.c
+++ b/src/SDCCcse.c
@@ -493,9 +493,14 @@ DEFSETFUNC (findPointerSet)
   V_ARG (operand **, opp);
   V_ARG (operand *, rop);
 
+  /* A read through a pointer to a volatile object has to happen, whatever was stored before. */
+  if (IS_PTR (operandType (op)) && isVolatile (operandType (op)->next))
+    return 0;
+
   if (POINTER_SET (cdp->diCode) &&
       op->key &&
       IC_RESULT (cdp->diCode)->key == op->key &&
+      !(IS_PTR (operandType (IC_RESULT (cdp->diCode))) && isVolatile (operandType (IC_RESULT (cdp->diCode))->next)) &&
       !isOperandVolatile (IC_RESULT (cdp->diCode), true) &&
       !isOperandVolatile (IC_RIGHT (cdp->diCode), true) &&
       getSize (operandType (IC_RIGHT (cdp->diCode))) ==
